    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d443-a1">

                <pb facs="0543" n="459" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg459"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Lord Lansdowne to Mr. White.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-12-17"><hi rendition="#italic">December 17,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 13th instant, stating, with reference to the proposal of the
                    German Government for a pacific blockade of the Venezuelan harbors, that the
                    United States Government do not acquiesce in any extension of the doctrine of
                    pacific blockade which may adversely affect the right of States not parties to
                    the controversy or discriminate against the commerce of neutral nations. You add
                    that the United States Government reserve all their rights in connection with
                    the matter.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansdowne.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
